From 0b75af957c1b3cc8adbf559a7ce2fe6f6e8d30d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:53:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/52] M4.1: render-target identity + depth bindings in the
 frame dump

Step one of the per-eye render rewrite. Before the design can be made, the
pass graph has to be known: how many distinct full-size targets exist, the
order they are bound, which are ping-ponged by post-processing, and which one
carries the image that reaches the screen. Size alone cannot answer that -
half the targets in a UE3 frame share a size - so every surface gets a stable
ID the first time it is seen and the dump prints IDs.

Every duplicated pass in the rewrite needs a right-eye twin, and a shared
depth buffer between eyes is one of the ways a naive rewrite breaks, so depth
bindings are logged too.
---
 src/d3d9/d3d9_device.cpp | 322 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 subprojects/.wraplock    |   0
 2 files changed, 286 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 subprojects/.wraplock

